.TH geectl-local-build-wipe 1  "geectl-local-build-wipe 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-local\-build\-wipe \- Wipe a build root: delete its contents (the lock file stays). A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the wipe. The marker check and the in\-use lock are safety invariants, never bypassed
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl local\-build wipe\fR [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-flavor\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIREPO\fR] [\fIARCH\fR] [\fISPEC\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wipe a build root: delete its contents (the lock file stays). A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the wipe. The marker check and the in\-use lock are safety invariants, never bypassed
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The OBS project the package belongs to. Required unless `\-\-root` names the root directly
.TP
\fB\-\-flavor\fR \fI<FLAVOR>\fR
The multibuild flavor; required when the source carries a `_multibuild` file
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
The root to wipe, named directly. Conflicts with the coordinates: when set, the root is wiped as named
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIREPO\fR]
The repository the root was built for. Required unless `\-\-root` names the root directly
.TP
[\fIARCH\fR]
The architecture the root was built for. Required unless `\-\-root` names the root directly
.TP
[\fISPEC\fR]
The source directory (spec + sources); the package comes from the spec file in it, like the build. Required unless `\-\-root` names the root directly
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
